transcript:
Excellent question! Yes, the current approach supports this pattern perfectly. Let me show you a minimal example of how this would work with the enhanced modules.

## Example: Leads Bounded Context + Public API

### Bounded Context Module (Business Logic)

**File: `modules/bounded_contexts/leads/application/lambda_api_public_create_lead.tf`**

```hcl
module "create_lead_lambda" {
  source = "git::https://github.com/Comecacahuates/terraform-modules.git//lambda/go?ref=v1.5.0"

  function_name = "sicadcam-${var.environment}-leads-api-create-lead"
  source_file   = "${var.lambda_packages_dir}/leads_api_create_lead.zip"

  memory_size = 128
  timeout     = 5

  environment_variables = {
    ENVIRONMENT   = var.environment
    TABLE_NAME    = var.dynamodb_table.name
    SNS_TOPIC_ARN = var.sns_topic_arn
  }

  policy_statements = [
    {
      Action   = ["dynamodb:PutItem"]
      Resource = [var.dynamodb_table.arn]
    },
    {
      Action   = ["sns:Publish"]
      Resource = [var.sns_topic_arn]
    }
  ]

  api_gateway_validation_schema = jsonencode({
    type     = "object"
    required = ["name", "email", "message"]
    properties = {
      name    = { type = "string", minLength = 1 }
      email   = { type = "string", pattern = "^[^@]+@[^@]+\\.[^@]+$" }
      message = { type = "string", minLength = 10 }
    }
  })

  tags = var.tags
}
```

**File: `modules/bounded_contexts/leads/application/outputs.tf`**

```hcl
output "lambda_api_create_lead" {
  value = {
    function_name      = module.create_lead_lambda.function_name
    function_arn       = module.create_lead_lambda.function_arn
    invoke_arn         = module.create_lead_lambda.invoke_arn
    validation_schema  = module.create_lead_lambda.api_gateway_validation_schema
  }
}
```

### API Module (Infrastructure)

**File: `modules/apis/public/main.tf`**

```hcl
module "public_api" {
  source = "git::https://github.com/Comecacahuates/terraform-modules.git//api-gateway/rest-api?ref=v1.5.0"

  api_name    = "sicadcam-${var.environment}-public-api"
  environment = var.environment

  deployment_triggers = {
    leads_create = var.lambda_api_create_lead.invoke_arn
  }

  tags = var.tags
}

# Request validator
resource "aws_api_gateway_request_validator" "body" {
  rest_api_id           = module.public_api.api_id
  name                  = "validate-body"
  validate_request_body = true
}

# POST /leads
module "create_lead_endpoint" {
  source = "git::https://github.com/Comecacahuates/terraform-modules.git//api-gateway/endpoint?ref=v1.5.0"

  api_id            = module.public_api.api_id
  parent_id         = module.public_api.root_resource_id
  path_part         = "leads"
  http_method       = "POST"
  api_execution_arn = module.public_api.execution_arn

  lambda_invoke_arn    = var.lambda_api_create_lead.invoke_arn
  lambda_function_name = var.lambda_api_create_lead.function_name

  request_validator_id = aws_api_gateway_request_validator.body.id
  request_model_schema = var.lambda_api_create_lead.validation_schema

  cors_origin  = var.cors_allowed_origin
  cors_methods = "POST,OPTIONS"

  tags = var.tags
}
```

**File: `modules/apis/public/variables.tf`**

```hcl
variable "environment" {
  type = string
}

variable "lambda_api_create_lead" {
  type = object({
    function_name     = string
    invoke_arn        = string
    validation_schema = string
  })
}

variable "cors_allowed_origin" {
  type = string
}

variable "tags" {
  type = map(string)
}
```

## Analysis

**✅ Pros:**
- **Clean separation**: Business logic (bounded context) vs infrastructure (API)
- **Concise**: Lambda handler = ~30 lines, API endpoint = ~20 lines
- **Type-safe**: Validation schema flows from bounded context to API
- **Reusable**: Both modules use your reusable terraform-modules
- **DDD-aligned**: Bounded contexts are self-contained

**✅ What's Good:**
- Bounded context outputs everything API needs (invoke_arn, validation_schema)
- API module just wires things together
- No duplication of validation schemas
- Easy to add more endpoints (just add more `module "endpoint"` blocks)

**⚠️ Potential Improvement:**

If you find yourself repeating the endpoint pattern, you could create a **higher-level module** like `api-gateway/validated-endpoint` that combines endpoint + validator + model:

```hcl
module "create_lead_endpoint" {
  source = "git::...//api-gateway/validated-endpoint?ref=v1.5.0"

  api_id       = module.public_api.api_id
  parent_id    = module.public_api.root_resource_id
  path_part    = "leads"
  http_method  = "POST"

  lambda       = var.lambda_api_create_lead  # Pass entire object
  cors_origin  = var.cors_allowed_origin
}
```

This would reduce the API module to ~10 lines per endpoint.

**Would you like me to create this `validated-endpoint` wrapper module?** It would make the API module even more concise while keeping the bounded context module unchanged.
